      "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-80722: the fifth Taylor coefficient is f^(5)(-2)/5!, so the derivative is 13·120=1560. q-69833: ZX=(1,1,0) and ZY=(0,3,0), giving cosine 1/√2 and angle 45°. q-101509: PQ=(2,-2,-1) and PR=(0,1,1), giving cosine -1/√2 and angle 135°. q-117441: splitting the absolute-value integral at x=1 gives areas 2 and 18, totaling 20. q-42438: arctan has domain all real numbers, so all three values qualify. q-117338: its range is (-π/2,π/2); -5π/6 is outside, while the other choices are inside. q-142835: sec²x=1+tan²x makes the numerator equal the denominator, yielding 1 wherever the original expression is defined. q-115699: image option 4 decreases throughout [-4,-1], so right-endpoint rectangles underestimate. q-84843: eliminating t from option 1 gives (y-2)²=-4(x+4), with vertex (-4,2), opening left and passing through (-5,4); unrestricted t generates the entire parabola. q-126510: c·d=4-4=0, so the projection is the zero vector. q-115698: image option 2 decreases throughout [-1,1], giving a right-sum underestimate. q-115737: width 3 and right endpoints -3,0,3 give 3(5-2+k)=6, hence k=-1. q-23847: sin²x+cos²x=1 and 1+tan²x=sec²x. q-120637: substituting sec²θ=1+tan²θ yields 2tan²θ. q-11615: the binomial coefficients give 1+x/2-x²/8+x³/16. q-125340: the nth term is x^(2n+1)/(2n+1), starting at n=0. The stray opening brace in q-84843's intermediate system is a formatting defect and does not alter its correct mathematics.",
